CutLocal is an independent C#/.NET implementation. It does not bundle or run
the rembg Python package. The rembg project was used as a documented technical
reference for compatible model preprocessing, postprocessing, and model asset
distribution. rembg is Copyright (c) 2020-present Daniel Gatis and is licensed
under the MIT License.

The default U2NetP model originates from the U-2-Net project, licensed under
Apache-2.0. The optional BiRefNet General Lite codebase is MIT-licensed, but the
reviewed model weight is conservatively classified as non-commercial because a
clear weight-specific permissive grant was not identified. Exact artifact
sources, hashes, versions, and distribution decisions are recorded in
assets/models/manifests and ThirdPartyNotices.txt.

Full dependency, model, copyright, and license notices are available in
ThirdPartyNotices.txt and assets/licenses.
